{
  "title": "Scholarship Scheme Progress by District",
  "subtitle": "Overview of application status and pending cases across districts",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Applications",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Pending Cases",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending'",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Pending Percentage",
      "sql": "SELECT (COUNT(*) * 100.0 / NULLIF(SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Pending' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) + SUM(CASE WHEN \"Status\" != 'Pending' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), 0)) AS pct FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
      "unit": "%"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Applications by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS total_apps FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "District",
      "y": ["total_apps"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Pending Cases by District",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", COUNT(*) AS pending_count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Status\" = 'Pending' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "District",
      "y": ["pending_count"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "District Status Breakdown",
      "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"Status\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1, 2 ORDER BY 1, 3 DESC"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard provides a comprehensive view of the scholarship scheme's progress, segmented by district. The total number of applications received is {{p1}}, serving as the baseline for all subsequent analysis.\n\nA critical focus area is the number of pending cases, which currently stands at {{p2}}. This represents {{p3}} of the total applications, indicating the volume of work remaining before disbursement can be finalized.\n\nWhen analyzing the distribution of applications across districts, {{p4}} shows the total volume per region. However, the operational bottleneck is best visualized in {{p5}}, which highlights the specific districts with the highest number of pending cases. For a granular view of how each district is performing across all statuses, refer to the detailed breakdown in {{p6}}."
}

{
  "title": "Child Fitness Progress Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Comparing baseline and endline performance metrics across locations and coaches",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Children Assessed",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM (SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"baseline\" UNION ALL SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"endline\") t",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run Change",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS change FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\"",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Sit-ups Gain by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Location\", AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS sit_ups_gain FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 15",
      "x": "Location",
      "y": ["sit_ups_gain"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Shuttle Run Improvement by Coach",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Coach\", AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS shuttle_improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 15",
      "x": "Coach",
      "y": ["shuttle_improvement"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top Locations by Overall Fitness Gain",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Location\", AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS sit_ups_gain, AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS shuttle_gain FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY sit_ups_gain DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard tracks the physical progress of children from baseline to endline. The total number of unique children assessed is {{p1}}. On average, participants improved their sit-up count by {{p2}}, indicating better core strength. Conversely, a positive value in {{p3}} would indicate slower times, but since this metric represents seconds, a negative value here signifies faster running times and thus improvement. When analyzing by location, the top performers in sit-ups are shown in {{p4}}, highlighting regional strengths. Similarly, {{p5}} breaks down running speed improvements by coach, helping identify which training methods yielded the best results for shuttle runs."
}

{
  "title": "Fitness Programme Results",
  "subtitle": "Summary of participant growth and performance by location and coach",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total Participants",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM (SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"baseline\" UNION ALL SELECT \"Child ID\" FROM \"endline\")",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS n FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Avg Height Gain (cm)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(e.\"Height cm\" - b.\"Height cm\") AS n FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Height cm\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Height cm\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": "cm"
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Sit-ups by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Location\", AVG(\"Sit ups\") AS avg_situps FROM \"endline\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
      "x": "Location",
      "y": ["avg_situps"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Avg Shuttle Run by Coach",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Coach\", AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_shuttle FROM \"endline\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 ASC LIMIT 10",
      "x": "Coach",
      "y": ["avg_shuttle"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 5 Locations by Participation",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Location\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM (SELECT \"Location\" FROM \"baseline\" UNION ALL SELECT \"Location\" FROM \"endline\") GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 5"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The programme engaged a total of {{p1}} participants across multiple locations. On average, participants improved their sit-up count by {{p2}} repetitions, demonstrating significant gains in core strength. Physical growth was also observed, with an average height increase of {{p3}} cm recorded between baseline and endline measurements. Performance varied by location, with the top performing sites for sit-ups averaging {{p4.0}} repetitions. Coaching effectiveness was also tracked, where the fastest average shuttle run times were recorded under {{p5.0}}. The most active locations by participant volume are detailed in the table below."
}

{
  "title": "Gender Improvement Comparison",
  "subtitle": "Comparing physical performance gains between female and male participants",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Female Avg Improvement (Sit-ups)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Female' AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Male Avg Improvement (Sit-ups)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Male' AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Female Avg Improvement (Shuttle)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Female' AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Male Avg Improvement (Shuttle)",
      "sql": "SELECT AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS improvement FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Male' AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Improvement by Gender and Metric",
      "sql": "SELECT 'Sit-ups' AS metric, AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_change FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Female' AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'Sit-ups', AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Male' AND e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'Shuttle', AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Female' AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'Shuttle', AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE b.\"Gender\" = 'Male' AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL",
      "x": "metric",
      "y": ["avg_change"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p6",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Detailed Gender Breakdown",
      "sql": "SELECT b.\"Gender\", COUNT(*) AS count, AVG(b.\"Sit ups\" - e.\"Sit ups\") AS situp_change, AVG(b.\"Shuttle run sec\" - e.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS shuttle_change FROM \"baseline\" b JOIN \"endline\" e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" WHERE e.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Sit ups\" IS NOT NULL AND e.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL AND b.\"Shuttle run sec\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "To determine if girls and boys are improving equally, we analyzed the change in physical metrics between baseline and endline data. The average improvement in sit-ups for female participants is {{p1}}, while male participants showed an average improvement of {{p2}}. This suggests a difference in strength endurance gains between the two groups.\n\nWhen examining speed via the shuttle run, female participants improved by an average of {{p3}} seconds, whereas male participants improved by {{p4}} seconds. A negative value indicates a reduction in time, which is an improvement in speed.\n\nThe bar chart visualizes these disparities across both metrics, highlighting whether one gender is outperforming the other in specific areas. The detailed table provides the exact counts and average changes for each gender, allowing for a granular comparison of progress."
}

